cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HABIT in scientific work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "HABIT: Habitat Analysis - Biomedical Imaging Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  HABIT is an open-source toolkit for tumour habitat analysis and intratumoral
  heterogeneity quantification. It covers image preprocessing, voxel-level
  feature construction, supervoxel and population-level habitat clustering,
  habitat-level feature extraction (including multiregional spatial interaction
  and intratumoral heterogeneity scores), and downstream machine-learning
  modelling and evaluation.
type: software
